bug_report:
[12 Regression] checking ICE when substituting packs into type aliases
GCC trunk currently ICEs for the following code

template <class... Ts> struct X {
  template <class... Us> using Y = X<void(Ts, Us)...>;
};

template <class A, class... P>
using any_pairs_list_4 = X<int, int>::Y<A, P...>;

int main() {
  any_pairs_list_4<int, int> array;
}

This seems to be a trunk regression because GCC 14 works fine (see godbolt linkhttps://godbolt.org/z/r6c7TcvcW)
